Emoji: bundle NotoColorEmoji and name it as a fallback family.

Every emoji in keklist rendered as .notdef on the Vita. The cause is not
keklist's font choice -- it declares no fonts at all -- but the port's font
situation, and it cannot be fixed on the port side alone:

  * app0:/fonts holds exactly one file, Roboto-Regular.ttf. 896 codepoints,
    nothing above U+FFFD, no emoji, not one codepoint >= U+1F000. That is the
    entire system font pool, so every app on this port renders emoji as tofu.

  * SkFontMgr_Custom::onMatchFamilyStyleCharacter returns nullptr
    (skia/src/ports/SkFontMgr_custom.cpp). That is the hook Skia calls to find
    a font for a codepoint the current family lacks, so there is NO automatic
    per-character fallback on this port. Installing an emoji font into
    app0:/fonts would therefore fix nothing by itself -- the family has to be
    named by the application.

So the fix is app-side by necessity: bundle the font and name it in
fontFamilyFallback. NotoColorEmoji.ttf is copied from the engine checkout,
which already ships it beside the Roboto the port uses:

  cp third_party/flutter/engine/src/flutter/txt/third_party/fonts/NotoColorEmoji.ttf \
     apps/corpus/keklist/assets/fonts/

It is 4.7 MB and takes the .vpk from 18 MB to 22 MB.

Colour works. The font is CBDT/CBLC -- PNG bitmaps, no glyf outlines -- and the
engine's FreeType is built with FT_CONFIG_OPTION_USE_PNG,
TT_CONFIG_OPTION_EMBEDDED_BITMAPS and TT_CONFIG_OPTION_COLOR_LAYERS, so the
emoji picker renders in full colour with skin-tone variants on hardware.

mind_widget names the family directly rather than relying on the fallback: it
draws nothing but the emoji, and the commented-out line doing exactly this was
already there. Note that the empty-state emoji still looks grey -- that is
MindCollectionEmptyStateWidget's own ColorFilter.matrix greyscale, by design,
not a rendering failure.

